  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining Peacebuilding and Increasing Community Resilience in the Eastern Libyan Municipalities of Benghazi and Derna</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The joint project aims to strengthen long term peacebuilding efforts and enhance community resilience across the Eastern Libyan municipalities of Benghazi and Derna. Its core focus is to support inclusive, participatory and collaborative approaches that bring together local authorities, civil society, and community members to shape recovery priorities and build a shared vision for stability. The initiative seeks to rebuild trust, reduce tensions, and promote social cohesion in areas that have experienced prolonged conflict and disruption. A central component of the project is the development of sustainable livelihood opportunities, with particular attention to women, youth, and marginalized groups who often face the greatest barriers to economic participation. Through targeted skills development, entrepreneurship support, and community driven economic initiatives, the project intends to expand access to income generating activities and strengthen household resilience. These efforts are designed not only to improve economic well being but also to empower individuals to play an active role in shaping peaceful and resilient communities. Overall, the project combines peacebuilding, recovery planning, and livelihood creation to help communities in Benghazi and Derna move toward a more stable, inclusive, and self reliant future.</narrative>
  </description>
